  "narrative": "The newly delivered scheduled validation directly supports the positive TP53-loss claim. H13's independent validation gives a signed TP53-loss estimate of +0.356 with a conservative independent interval from +0.214 to +0.498. Both the point estimate and lower bound exceed the 0.15-unit threshold, so TP53 loss remains accepted as a strong within-dataset association with higher dependency_composite values, i.e. weaker composite dependency. H13 is therefore accepted and closed. The validation for H18 is a clean negative result: in the KEAP1-intact population, STK11 loss has a signed estimate of only +0.024, with an interval from -0.087 to +0.135. This is far below the threshold and the interval includes zero; it does not support a scientifically meaningful association of STK11 loss with stronger dependency. H18 is rejected and closed. These validations also reduce the concern that the main landscape is driven by technical or platform artifacts, because the major effects remain distinct even when STK11-loss and other contexts are tested separately.\n\nThe current supported within-dataset landscape is now broad and internally coherent. KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss are associated with higher, less negative dependency_composite values, meaning weaker composite dependency. SMARCA4 loss and PTEN loss are associated with lower, more negative values, meaning stronger composite dependency. KEAP1 and SMARCA4 are extremely robust after stringent central-loss exclusion, high-quality-screen restriction, and adenocarcinoma restriction. TP53 is independently validated and robust across central-loss-excluded contexts. PTEN is accepted from its validated main effect and several robust contexts, although some narrower context estimates remain closer to the threshold. Negative or unsupported claimed associations include KRAS mutation, MYC amplification, EGFR amplification, PIK3CA mutation, ARID1A loss in the claimed stronger-dependency direction, STK11 loss in the claimed stronger-dependency direction, RB1 loss in the claimed weaker-dependency direction, SMAD4 loss, APC mutation, BRAF V600E, the constructed research markers, MTAP in central-loss-excluded contexts, ERBB2 amplification, BRCA2 loss, NF1 loss, media serum difference, CRISPR library offset, and matched omics-availability offset.\n\nThe major data-driven refinement is MSI-high. The originally registered positive-direction claims were rejected because the observed signed estimates were large and negative. The corresponding reverse claims now have the appropriately signed evidence. H120 gives a signed overall MSI-high effect of +0.792, interval +0.676 to +0.907, and H121 gives a signed effect of +0.754, interval +0.683 to +0.825, after excluding TP53, SMARCA4, KEAP1, and PTEN loss. Both are far beyond the threshold in the reverse direction. I therefore accept and keep active H120 and H121: MSI-high cells have substantially lower, more negative dependency_composite values, meaning stronger composite dependency, and this pattern is not explained by the four central losses. This is still a supplied-dataset association, not a causal effect, not a single-gene knockout measurement, and not a claim of external generalizability. The next priority is to understand where the MSI-high effect is robust and whether it is modified by lineage subtype, mutation burden, high-quality screens, or co-occurrence with TP53 loss. Proposed analyses focus on these contexts, with formal interactions to distinguish a broadly present association from genuine effect modification.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 6 synthesis update: H13 accepted/closed with independent validation (signed +0.356, lower +0.214). H18 rejected/closed with validation (signed +0.024, interval -0.087 to +0.135). The broad secondary/technical screen is largely null for claimed directions: ERBB2, BRCA2, NF1, MTAP/CDKN2A contexts, media serum, Avana library, and matched RNA/DNA do not support threshold-level offsets.\n\nAccepted landscape: KEAP1 loss -> higher/less negative dependency_composite (weaker dependency); TP53 loss -> higher/less negative dependency_composite (weaker dependency); SMARCA4 loss -> lower/more negative dependency_composite (stronger dependency); PTEN loss -> lower/more negative dependency_composite (stronger dependency). CDKN2A remains unresolved/closed low priority due to validation below threshold. MTAP is not independently supported.\n\nNew accepted post-hoc reversal: MSI-high -> lower/more negative dependency_composite (stronger dependency). H120 main accepted active (signed +0.792, lower +0.676); H121 central-loss-intact accepted active (signed +0.754, lower +0.683). Both far exceed threshold. Keep active to test validation and context robustness.\n\nNext analyses: MSI-high high-quality screens, central-loss-intact adenocarcinoma, MSI-high interaction by lineage_subtype, MSI-high high mutation burden, MSI-high interaction by high mutation burden, and MSI-high interaction by TP53 loss among other central losses excluded. If a context is robust, consider validation at appraise; if interactions are modest, favor a broadly present MSI-high association rather than a subtype-specific claim. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
}
